-- ============================================================================
-- Data Type Justification
-- ============================================================================

-- [Id]: INT IDENTITY - Standard surrogate key, supports up to 2.1 billion records
-- [Title]: NVARCHAR(255) - Unicode support for international characters
-- [Description]: NVARCHAR(MAX) - Flexible length for detailed descriptions
-- [Priority], [Status]: INT - Enum values; ordinal comparison for sorting/filtering
-- [CreatedById], [AssignedToId]: INT - Foreign key references to Users table
-- [CreatedAt], [AssignedAt], [StartedAt], [ResolvedAt], [ClosedAt]: DATETIME2 - Precision to 100 nanoseconds
-- [RowVersion]: ROWVERSION - Automatic concurrency control by SQL Server

-- ============================================================================
-- Notes for Database Administration
-- ============================================================================

-- 1. FOREIGN KEYS:
--    - CreatedById: RESTRICT prevents deletion of users who created issues (maintains referential integrity)
--    - AssignedToId: SET NULL allows deletion of users by clearing their assignments gracefully

-- 2. CONCURRENCY:
--    - RowVersion (ROWVERSION datatype) is automatically updated by SQL Server on each row modification
--    - Use in application: SELECT current RowVersion on read, include in WHERE clause on update
--    - Prevents lost updates in concurrent scenarios

-- 3. AUDIT TRAIL:
--    - CreatedAt: Set automatically to UTC time, never changes
--    - AssignedAt, StartedAt, ResolvedAt, ClosedAt: Application should set based on business logic
--    - All timestamps in UTC for consistency across time zones

-- 4. DEFAULTS:
--    - Priority defaults to Normal (1)
--    - Status defaults to New (0)
--    - CreatedAt defaults to current UTC time
--    - This allows inserts with minimal required parameters

-- 5. INDEXES:
--    - 7 indexes optimized for common query patterns
--    - Covering indexes include frequently selected columns to enable index-only scans
--    - Composite indexes support both single-column and multi-column filters

